(163, 1, '2024-10-11 15:45:46', '2024-10-11 15:45:46', '<!-- wp:columns -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":162,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img src=\"https://pjacobsen.bitlampsites.com/wpd/Final/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/pup-2.webp\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-162\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column -->\n\n<!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><br>A boisterous wolf pup and an awkward young porcupine are unlikely allies in this tale of friendship set on Alaska’s tundra. The two grow up as neighbors, but only through helping each other escape from a trapper do they learn what it means truly to be friends.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column --></div>\n<!-- /wp:columns -->', 'Pup and Pokey', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '160-revision-v1', '', '', '2024-10-11 15:45:46', '2024-10-11 15:45:46', '', 160, 'https://pjacobsen.bitlampsites.com/wpd/Final/?p=163', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(164, 1, '2024-10-11 15:48:22', '2024-10-11 15:48:22', '<!-- wp:columns -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns\"><!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:image {\"id\":165,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img src=\"https://pjacobsen.bitlampsites.com/wpd/Final/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/porcupine-1.webp\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-165\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column -->\n\n<!-- wp:column -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-column\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>“Seth Kantner illuminates an Alaska most of us will never know.”</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><br><em><strong>– Andrea Barrett, author of Ship Fever and</strong></em></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><em><strong>The Voyage of the Narwhal</strong></em></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>“Suspense and heartache are matched by wry humor and outrage, and all is infused with Kantner’s humility and deep respect for the wild…Crafted with the precision and nerve acquired by living off the land, this is a powerful and important book of remembrance, protest, and warning.”</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><br><em><strong>– Booklist</strong></em></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:column --></div>\n<!-- /wp:columns -->', 'Shopping for Porcupine', '', 'publish', 'closed', 'closed', '', '164-2', '', '', '2024-10-11 15:48:39', '2024-10-11 15:48:39', '', 0, 'https://pjacobsen.bitlampsites.com/wpd/Final/?post_type=book&#038;p=164', 0, 'book', '', 0),
